00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.202
that this really came down to creativity.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.069
Ed Sheeran saying

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:50.970
if he can't

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.639
have that four chord progression,

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:53.840
he can't be creative.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.843
What do you make of this verdict?

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.579
Yeah, I'm not surprised by the verdict.

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:00.613
Very difficult case.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:01.080
Obviously,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.348
the Townsend family felt

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:05.451
very passionate that Ed Sheeran had

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:06.419
a, you know,

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.555
use the four chord progression

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:09.956
that was in the song

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:11.391
that was

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:12.392
co-written with Marvin

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:14.294
Gaye by their father.

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:15.662
But I think what was impactful

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:16.963
for the jury was that Ed

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:17.664
Sheeran was able

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:18.331
to put on evidence

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.165
that this for chord

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.667
progression was used in songs

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.502
even before Marvin Gaye.

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:23.937
And Townsend

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:25.805
recorded that very popular song

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.340
by Marvin Gaye.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.309
And I think that had a big impact

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:29.909
on this jury,

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.311
because ultimately,

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.278
if the court

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:32.812
the four chord

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.681
